  <div class="wrap page-intro"><p class="eyebrow">About this companion</p><h1>Site notices.</h1><p class="lead">Publication attribution, the operation of this website, and where to take questions about the book.</p></div>
  <article class="wrap narrow prose notices"><section id="privacy"><h2>Privacy Notice</h2><p>This version of the companion does not include analytics scripts, advertising, embedded video players, account registration, or a contact form. Chapter and contributor filtering happens in your browser. Search terms appear in the page address so that a filtered view can be shared; they are not sent to a separate search service by the site’s code. Copies of the displayed cover and identity images are served with the website rather than requested from the original image services on each visit.</p><p>Your connection still makes ordinary requests to the website’s hosting infrastructure. Hosting and network providers may process request information under their own practices. Following a link to a publisher or another website takes you to a separate service. Do not place sensitive or operational information in a search term or a shared page address.</p></section><section id="cookies"><h2>Cookie Settings</h2><p>The companion’s application code does not set cookies or use browser local storage. There are no optional tracking features to enable or disable in this version, so there is no consent toggle that pretends to control something the site does not use. Browser and hosting-provider behavior is separate from the application code described here. These notices should be reviewed if analytics, embedded services, or other data-collecting features are introduced.</p></section><section id="terms"><h2>Terms of Use</h2><p>This is a scholarly companion to the handbook. Chapter pages identify contributions and their sources; they do not reproduce the chapter texts. Reading notes and discussion exercises are original companion-site material, clearly distinguished from the authors’ contributions. They are intended for reading and teaching, not for making operational decisions. Publication access, purchases, and reuse permissions should be checked with the publisher or the relevant rights holder.</p><p>To report a correction, contact <a href="https://www.drnataliescala.com/">Natalie Scala</a> or <a href="https://jameshoward.us/">James Howard</a> through their websites. Identify the edition, chapter, and source of the correction so that an earlier-edition record is not inadvertently changed to match a later one.</p></section><section id="copyright"><h2>Copyright</h2><p>Copyright © 2018–{new Date().getFullYear()} Natalie M. Scala and James P. Howard, II, for original companion-site material. The handbook, its individual chapters, cover artwork, photographs, and other third-party material retain their respective rights and attribution. Display here does not imply that the site owners hold every right in every item. No blanket reuse license for the book or its illustrations is granted by this website.</p></section></article>
